 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? About six months before the big day. That way, there's time to book the venue, hire band or caterer, and get your guests to start thinking about the day. August is lovely, but can be busy. Is there a quieter month you' like? Most couples mix both. A few postcards in the postmark add an extra touch. Classic. For the guests, the save the date is just polite reminder with dates. The real wedding invitation is where you ask them to come. You can keep it simple or go all out. A handwritten hand address and a gold foil stamp looks stunning.",
